Z||000000||gkozlov||07-17-2000||10:56 AM||||It's a 86 SE.<BR>1. I seem to get average 15-16 mpg. Ive heard of the 2.8 getting @ 20 mpg.<BR>2. I was under the impression that my car had a 10.5 gallon gas tank. Earlier today I ran out of gas pulling into a gas station and could only squeeze in 9 gallons in.<BR>3.My gas guage is off. When full it reads a little more than .75 full. Is there a simple fix?<BR>4. My car sits about an inch higher than my buddies stock 87 coupe. Whats up with that?<BR>For the ride height I've got pics of my car posted here <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002922.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002922.html</A>  <P>Thanks in advance. <BR>gkozlov<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||07-17-2000||01:32 PM||||the 87 may either have lower profile tires or slightly lower factory springs or both. You can run the RPO code from the lable in the left fender and see if it's got one of the "handling packages." My 87SC has one of the pakcages and is far stiffer than base coupes w/o it. I never checked the hight, but then I also put 70 series tires on so it's going to be lower than stock.<P>9 gallons into a 10.5 tank is about normal if you didn't run it stone dry. (Don't EVER allow it to run dry. You can ruin the fuel pump.)<P>Milage can be any number of things.<P>Fiero Fuel gauges are commonly flaky. Live with it or drop the tank. It's a sender problem most of the time. Mine is batty to. As long as the left half of the gauge works right I don't care that it seldom/never says full. I just don't want to be running dry and wreck the pump. When mine says empty you better be heading for a filling station.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||07-17-2000||09:30 PM||||I have an 86 GT with 2.8 engine. I also only get about 14-15 mpg city. When I take it out on the highway, I can get it to the factory specs for mpg. But then I hit city and the milage die, worse then 14-15 for a while. My gas guage reads full when I fill up, and I think its okay. I am going to replace the sensor and sending unit anyway. It couldnt hurt. Let me know if anyone has any idea about why the car is getting bad milage. Thanks<P>sean@kdsi.net<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||07-17-2000||09:45 PM||||I took 2 trips in june of 1,500 each.  On both trips i got 24 mpg average on the entire trip each.  I have an 86 GT with 2.8 automatic.||||reg||1
