Z||000010||wxxo||07-18-2000||03:27 PM||||there was a thread posted some time ago about the fuel capacity. i was having a problem getting more than 8gal into my tank even when i knew that it was empty.( coasted into the gas station a time or two as well. cant believe how far these cars will coast...well thats another story altogether.)<BR>so i did what most people do. dropped the tank to see if there was a dead body in there taking up space where the gas is supposed to go. (that would have answered a few performance questions i have though) nothing wrong. the needle also always said 3/4 instead of full after i filled up. well all of these problems all come from a single fault in the piping to the tank. you have to dribble that last gallon or two in. it takes me 10 min to fill up my tank. pump shuts off hit it again. and again and again. i dont think that the 87 and 88s have this problem but that doesnt help us though.||||reg||1
